DEFENDANT META PLATFORMS, INC.’S RESPONSE IN OPPOSITION TO
PLAINTIFF’S MOTION FOR LEAVE TO FILE A SECOND AMENDED COMPLAINT
Defendant Meta Platforms, Inc., (“Meta”) by and through its undersigned counsel, hereby
respectfully opposes Plaintiff Marvelle J. Ballentine’s Motion for Leave to File a Second Amended
Complaint (Dkt. No. 114). In support, Meta states as follows:
I.
PROCEDURAL HISTORY
As described in Meta’s Motion to Dismiss the First Amended Complaint (“FAC”), Plaintiff
filed a series of actions against Meta across several courts, all stemming from the alleged
disablement of his Facebook account. See Dkt. No. 22 at 3-5. Across these actions, Plaintiff has
routinely filed amended complaints (or sought leave to do so), consistently delaying decisions on
motions to dismiss. Indeed, since September 9, 2025, when Plaintiff filed his first complaint
against Meta in the United States District Court for the Northern District of California, Plaintiff
has filed 12 complaints against Meta across four courts (not counting his proposed amended and
supplemental complaints in the instant action).
